   206                          ;; PUSHRETADDR and caml_APPLY n, APPLY1, APPLY2, APPLY3:
   207                          ;;
   208                          ;; A closure application to n arguments is usually compiled by ocamlc by
   209                          ;; emitting a PUSHRETADDR (which pushes the return address onto the stack),
   210                          ;; followed by instructions that compute and push the arguments, and finally an
   211                          ;; APPLY n instruction that jump to the closure code; but when n < 4, ocamlc
